<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Pappenheim</h1><p class="st-meta">1141 CE – 1806 CE (approx.) · capital Pappenheim</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Franconian lordship of the hereditary imperial marshals of Pappenheim, a family famous for the cavalry general of the Thirty Years' War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of Pappenheim, ministerials of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Staufer</a>, appear around 1141 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altmuhl">Altmühl</a> valley. They held the office of imperial marshal, later hereditary arch-marshal deputies to the Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, which gave the small family a prominent ceremonial role at coronations and diets.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lordship around the castle and town of Pappenheim was small, but the family's members served emperors widely. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim">Gottfried Heinrich of Pappenheim</a> was a leading imperial cavalry commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutzen-1632">Lützen</a> in 1632. The family became counts in 1628. The town converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Pappenheim was mediatised in 1806 and absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a>, though the counts kept their castle and estates. The marshal office ended with the dissolution of the Empire in 1806.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1141 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.41%;width:13.23%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1141 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pappenheim</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gottfried Heinrich of Pappenheim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, later Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian and Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Pappenheim, Pappenheim</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1474&amp;focus=lordship-of-pappenheim" aria-label="Lordship of Pappenheim on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4934 470 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Pappenheim lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5254 726L5229 694M5254 726L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5254 726h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5254 726h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pappenheim. <a href="/atlas?year=1474&amp;focus=lordship-of-pappenheim">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
